export declare const q1 = "<p>A celebrant is someone who officiates or leads a ceremony, such as a wedding, funeral, naming ceremony, or vow renewal. They work with people to create a ceremony that feels personal and meaningful.</p>";
export declare const q2 = "<p><b>No</b>, celebrancy in the UK is currently an unregulated industry, which means there\u2019s no legal requirement for formal training. In practice, this means anyone can offer celebrant services meaning standards and levels of experience can vary widely. I trained with the International College of Professional Celebrants, the UK\u2019s leading celebrant training provider. As a fully accredited member, I work to a clear set of professional standards and a code of practice and I am fully insured to work as a celebrant. I am also currently working towards my NOCN Double Platinum Diploma in Celebrancy, a nationally recognised qualification.</p>";
export declare const q3 = "\n            <p>The major difference is <b>legality</b> \u2013 Registrars are employed by the local councils to ensure marriages and civil partnerships are legally recognised. The ceremonies must take place in licensed venues and follow a strict legal script including the signing of the Marriage Register. </p>\n            <br>\n            <p>Celebrant led services are not legally binding so couples must complete a separate legal registration of marriage if they want it to be recognised by law. Many couples choose to separate the legal registration from their celebrant ceremony so they can focus on creating a relaxed, personal celebration without restrictions. Celebrant led ceremonies can be held absolutely anywhere and are free to include religious, spiritual or symbolic elements.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>Celebrant led ceremonies can be held absolutely anywhere and are free to include religious, spiritual or symbolic elements.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>In the UK, a legal marriage requires a simple statutory ceremony at a register office. This is often referred to as a \u201C2+2\u201D ceremony \u2014 just two witnesses, the couple, and a registrar completing the legal paperwork. It\u2019s a short, straightforward appointment that makes the marriage legally binding. Check <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/register-offices\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> to find your nearest Register Office and fees.</p>\n            ";
export declare const q4 = "\n            <p>Just as you are unique, so are celebrants!</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>It\u2019s important to choose one that is the right fit for you as a couple and for the type of service you want. You have to trust that they will tell <b>YOUR</b> story as you want and you need to be confident in their ability to lead the ceremony. Most couples know quickly if someone is right for them. If I\u2019m not the right fit for you, rest assured I will tell you and help guide you in a better direction.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>So, everything starts with a conversation. We\u2019ll have a free initial chat with no pressure and no obligations, just a chance for us to get to know each other, hear your story, and see if we're the right fit for each other. We can do this in person or online, whichever suits you.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>If we decide to work together, then we will meet up and I will ask you lots of questions! I want to know everything!! How you met, what makes you laugh, what defines your relationship, even your partner\u2019s superpower \u2013 everything that makes you two the couple you are. And I will ask you how you want your ceremony to feel.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>Now, when you book me as your celebrant, it's often many months, sometimes even eighteen months, before your wedding day. The truth is, life doesn't stand still while you're planning a wedding. Relationships grow, adventures happen, new memories are made, and sometimes priorities or ideas change too. The couple you are when you first book me may not be exactly the same couple standing in front of me on your wedding day, so I don\u2019t write it and put it away ready for the day. In the months leading up to your wedding, we'll work together to create a ceremony that reflects who you are <b>right now</b> \u2013 your story, your personalities, your values and the life you're building together. We'll chat, refine the details, add the little touches that make it uniquely yours, and make sure every word feels personal, meaningful and unmistakably you.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>We can rehearse the ceremony, talk through the flow of the day and make any final tweaks, ensuring you both feel relaxed, confident and excited. When you stand there and hear your ceremony, it should feel completely and unmistakably <b>you</b>. Not a template. Not a script written months ago. But a genuine reflection of your love story as it is in this moment. Because your ceremony deserves to tell the story of the couple you are today.</p>\n            ";
export declare const q5 = "<p>Of Course! This is your day and with a celebrant led service, you have no legal restrictions and no templates to follow. It's all about you and the celebration of your love story.</p>";
export declare const q6 = "\n            <p>If you're planning a summer wedding or ceremony, it's always best to book your celebrant as early as possible. Popular dates, especially weekends between May and September, can get snapped up very quickly, so securing your date sooner rather than later gives you peace of mind and plenty of time to create a ceremony that's perfect for you.</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>That said, if your ceremony is coming up sooner than expected, don't panic! It's always worth getting in touch. I may still have availability and would love to help make your special day unforgettable.</p>\n            ";
export declare const q7 = "<p>I live in East Devon and cover Exeter and the surrounding area as standard. However, I would happily officiate ceremonies anywhere in the South West. If your chosen venue is a little further afield, I may charge a small mileage fee to cover travel costs. Just let me know where you're planning your special day, and I'll be happy to provide a tailored quote. If you are thinking of other places in the UK or even a destination wedding, get in touch for a chat.</p>";
export declare const q8 = "To get details about my fees, get in touch for the details by using the contact form, or by emailing me.";
export declare const q9 = "\n            <p>Of course you can, but don\u2019t worry if you get stuck. I will always be there to support you!</p>\n            <br>\n            <p>Your vows are often the most personal and meaningful words you'll share on your wedding day. Some couples know exactly what they want to say, while others aren't sure where to begin and both are completely normal. If you'd like a little guidance, I'm here to help. Whether you write a few heartfelt sentences or something more detailed, I'll ensure your vows fit beautifully within your ceremony and that you feel confident sharing them on the day.</p>\n            ";
export declare const q10 = "<p>Bring them on!! As a keen Am Dram performer I am more than happy to don a costume and write an appropriate themed wedding.</p>";
